# Onboard parameters for Vehicle 1
#
# STAGE 5 - FLEET POLICY: arm switch on channel 7, kill switch on channel 5,
# FMU board mounted rotated 180 degrees (roll: upside down). Independent of vision, UART and
# the container. Loads on every FC.
#
# RC_MAP_ARM_SW = 7    arm/disarm switch is RC channel 7. PX4 v1.16: "Use it to
#                      arm/disarm via switch instead of default throttle stick. If
#                      this is assigned, arming and disarming via stick is disabled."
#                      The reference airframe's May-07 dump (and so 00_baseline.params
#                      until 2026-11-01) had arm on 5 and kill on 7, the other way
#                      round from the fleet's transmitter model setup. MAN_ARM_GESTURE
#                      is already 0 in the baseline. RC_ARMSWITCH_TH stays 0.75.
#
# RC_MAP_KILL_SW = 5   emergency kill switch is RC channel 5. RC_KILLSWITCH_TH stays
#                      0.75. Channels 5 and 7 are otherwise unused; flight mode is
#                      channel 6 (RC_MAP_FLTMODE, baseline).
#
# SENS_BOARD_ROT = 8   "Roll 180°" (v1.16.2 sensor_params.c: 0 No rotation, 4 Yaw 180°,
#                      8 Roll 180°, 12 Pitch 180°). Taken from drone 20's FC on 2026-11-01,
#                      the airframe the fleet radio/geometry files were read from and the
#                      value QGC's "Autopilot Orientation" was set to there: the Pixhawk 6C
#                      hangs upside down on these airframes (arrow forward, board inverted).
#                      If a build mounts it the right way up but facing the tail, that is
#                      4 (Yaw 180°) instead -- the two are not interchangeable. Reboot-
#                      gated. The level-horizon trim SENS_BOARD_X/Y/Z_OFF stays per-unit:
#                      run QGC's level horizon on each drone AFTER loading this file, with
#                      the rotation already in place, or the trim is measured in the
#                      wrong frame.
#
# All three are fleet-wide, not per-unit, but they are kept out of 00_baseline.params
# so that tools/param_diff.py --make-baseline still reproduces the baseline from the
# May-07 dump (selftest step 4). Reboot the FC after loading.
#
# Vehicle-Id	Component-Id	Name	Value	Type
1	1	RC_MAP_ARM_SW	7	6
1	1	RC_MAP_KILL_SW	5	6
1	1	SENS_BOARD_ROT	8	6
